ue processing please search open and closed issues before submitting a new one.\r\nExisting issues often contain information about workarounds, resolution, or progress updates.\r\n\r\n🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅-->\r\n\r\n# 📚 Docs or angular.io bug report\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\n<!-- ✍️edit:--> \r\nA snapshot and description for [the lifecycle hooks SpyDirective example](https://angular.io/guide/lifecycle-hooks#use-directives-to-watch-the-dom) doesn't match to an actual behavior.\r\n\r\n\r\n## 🔬 Minimal Reproduction\r\n\r\n### What's the affected URL?**\r\nhttps://angular.io/guide/lifecycle-hooks#use-directives-to-watch-the-dom\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Reproduction Steps**\r\n\r\n1. Go to https://angular.io/guide/lifecycle-hooks#use-directives-to-watch-the-dom\r\n2. Run the corresponding example in [Stackblitz](https://angular.io/generated/live-examples/lifecycle-hooks/stackblitz.html)\r\n3. In the live example click _Add Hero_ button. It adds Herbie \r\n4. Compare a log message sequence in the live example with the one in the docs. \r\nIn the docs' animation there's a # 3 event. But it's missed in the live example.\r\n\r\n### Expected vs Actual Behavior**\r\n**Actual**:  an animation for [the lifecycle hooks SpyDirective example](https://angular.io/guide/lifecycle-hooks#use-directives-to-watch-the-dom) doesn't match to an actual behavior.\r\n**Expected**: an animation for [the lifecycle hooks SpyDirective example](https://angular.io/guide/lifecycle-hooks#use-directives-to-watch-the-dom) matches to an actual behavior.\r\n\r\n## 📷Screenshot\r\n### In the docs\r\n![spy-directive](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/13061803/102643595-8d6ff780-4170-11eb-9328-661579d68e19.gif)\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n![ang_lifecycle](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/13061803/102643565-83e68f80-4170-11eb-8050-6024d43364da.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"AndrewKushnir","id":43554145,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTU0MTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercon